\section{Explore All Handoffs in a Two-Buffer Protocol Model}

A shutdown test can exercise interleavings systematically before a runtime implementation exists. Build an illustrative finite model with two named buffers. Record the free list, work queue, worker's holdings, and retired set separately, so a faulty transition could leave the same buffer in two places. The input includes an initial configuration and a transition generator implementing queue limits, cancellation, and release. Let retirement be legal only after stop has been requested. A terminal configuration has both stages stopped and both buffers retired. The checker below either finds no reachable stuck nonterminal configuration or ownership violation, or returns a shortest recorded counterexample to one of those checks.

\begin{verbatim}
check(initial):
  push initial into FIFO queue; seen = {initial}
  while queue is not empty:
    s = pop front of queue
    if not exactly_one_owner_per_buffer(s):
      return BadOwner(trace(s))
    succ = enabled_transitions(s)
    if succ is empty and not terminal(s):
      return Stuck(trace(s))
    for (event, t) in succ:
      # Remember the first, thus shortest, path to t.
      if t in seen: continue
      # Store the event even if it moves no buffer.
      parent[t] = (s, event)
      add t to seen; push t into queue
  return NoStuckState
\end{verbatim}

For a post-handoff fixture start with buffer \(A\) held by the worker and \(B\) free. Suppose the only transition is cancellation, which stops the producer and retires \(B\). If the worker's only release would be an unbuffered send back to the now stopped producer, nothing is enabled next. The checker returns \verb|Stuck([cancel])| even though \(A\) has exactly one owner. Add a worker transition that retires \(A\) after cancellation and stops the worker. With no other moves in this fixture, exploration reaches the terminal configuration and returns \texttt{NoStuckState}.

Figure~\ref{fig:visual-184} identifies the missing transition: the worker must be able to dispose of its buffer without cooperation from the stopped producer.

