The queue contains only reachable configurations and each unseen one is examined once. Breadth-first exploration costs space proportional to the number of distinct configurations, which grows quickly with real queue capacities and message contents. A cycle of enabled transitions in a model may still prevent eventual shutdown without yielding a stuck state. Checking that stronger property requires a progress argument or a cycle check under stated fairness assumptions.
